# 📖 TOEIC Grammar - Day 10

## Topic
# Infinitives vs. Gerunds
### (to + Verb / Verb + ing)

---

## 1. Infinitive (to + Verb)

Some verbs are followed by **to + verb**.

Examples

- I decided to study English.
- She hopes to get a new job.
- We plan to travel next month.

Common Verbs

- decide
- hope
- plan
- want
- need
- promise

---

## 2. Gerund (Verb + ing)

Some verbs are followed by **Verb + ing**.

Examples

- I enjoy studying English.
- He finished writing the report.
- She avoids driving at night.

Common Verbs

- enjoy
- finish
- avoid
- keep
- consider
- suggest

---

## Remember

| To + Verb | Verb + ing |
|------------|------------|
| decide | enjoy |
| hope | finish |
| plan | avoid |
| want | keep |
| promise | suggest |

---

## TOEIC Tip

✔ decide → to V

✔ enjoy → V-ing

시험에서는 동사 뒤에 오는 형태를 묻는 문제가 자주 출제된다.
